      "writtenOn": "2021-09-10T17:28:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not exactly. The implementation won\u0027t be custom. The purpose for this config is that you may need to call this probing logic after some preparations (like Keith said about enabling power rails) or depending on some other configs.\nMy main purpose for adding this config was based on lazor\u0027s cros code. There is a function that checks if current board is limozeen or lazor. If limozeen, then the sensors count is set to zero, otherwise, the call to probing sensor is done.\nThe same can be done in zephyr. Board logic can enable this config and create hook that will do internal checks and then call this generic probing code.",
